===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|literary}} The [[originator]] or [[creator]] of a [[work]], especially of a [[literary]] [[composition]]; or, one of the creators of a collaborative work.
#: {{ux|en|The copyright of any original writing belongs initially and properly to its '''author'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Have you read any Corinthian '''authors'''?}}
#: {{ux|en|This paper has three '''authors'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=III|passage=Eternal King; thee, '''Author''' of all being.|year=1873}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1661|author=[[w:John Fell (bishop)|John Fell]]|title=The Life of the most learned, reverend and pious Dr. H. Hammond|url=https://archive.org/details/a615775104worduoft|passage=During the whole time of his abode in the university he generally spent thirteen hours of the day in study; by which assiduity besides an exact dispatch of the whole course of philosophy, he read over in a manner all classic '''authors''' that are extant{{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Johnson Dictionary|chapter=Preface|passage=The chief glory of every people arises from its '''authors'''.}}
#* {{RQ:NYT|author=Catherine Pearson|title=She Started the Debate About Kids and Phones. Now She Wants to End It.|date=2025-09-06|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/09/06/well/family/jean-twenge-social-media-screens-teens.html|passage=[Jean] Twenge {{...|(pronounced TWANG-ee)}} isn’t necessarily a household name like her sometimes collaborator Jonathan Haidt, a social psychologist and the '''author''' of the megahit “The Anxious Generation,” which has spent 75 weeks hovering near the top of the New York Times best-seller list.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260221161400/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/09/06/well/family/jean-twenge-social-media-screens-teens.html|archivedate=21 February 2026}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=September 27, 2025|author=Julia Jacobo|title=Million-year-old skull could rewrite timeline of human origin, researchers say|work={{w|ABC News (United States)|ABC News}}|url=https://abcnews.go.com/International/million-year-skull-rewrite-timeline-human-origin-researchers/story?id=125964277|text="The cranium is clearly plesiomorphic in overall form, presenting primitive traits shared by earlier hominins," the '''authors''' wrote.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260214024329/https://abcnews.com/International/million-year-skull-rewrite-timeline-human-origin-researchers/story?id=125964277}}
# {{senseid|en|copyright}} {{lb|en|US|_|copyright law}} The [[initial]] owner of the copyright to a work, especially a work made for hire or a work of [[corporate]] authorship.
#: {{ux|en|The '''author''' named on the copyright registration for the Android robot is Google Inc.}}
# {{senseid|en|writer}} Someone who writes [[book]]s for a living.
# {{senseid|en|criminal}} {{lb|en|obsolete|criminal law}} [[principal|Principal]]; the [[primary]] [[participant]] in a [[crime]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1879|author=F. D. Morice|title=[[s:en:Pindar (Morice)|Pindar]]|publisher=[[s:Pindar (Morice)/Chapter 10|chapter 10]]|page=158|passage=We hear {{...|of banishments, of great houses suffering a temporary eclipse of their greatness, of savage feuds, and apparently—in dark and mysterious hints*—}}of fratricidal murders, and stern reprisals on their '''authors'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Case of Kieng Chek (Kham Muon) before the Franco-Siamese Mixed Court|year=1894|author=Franco-Siamese Mixed Court|location=Bangkok|publisher=n.p.|page=4|text=Accomplices of a crime or an offence shall incur the same punishment as the '''authors''' of such a crime or offence, except when the law will have disposed otherwise.|url=https://archive.org/download/caseofkiengchekk00franrich/caseofkiengchekk00franrich.pdf}}
# {{senseid|en|informant}} {{lb|en|archaic}} One's [[authority]] for something: an [[informant]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1699|title=Seven new Colloquies translated out of Erasmus
|passage=Let me inform you ''en passant'', Ladies, that those Villains the ''Heathens'', as my '''Authors''' tell me, (and I thought it wou'd{{sic}} not be amiss to communicate such a nice Observation to this House) used to call our Saviour ''Chrestus'', and not ''Christus'', by way of Contempt and Derision {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Stevenson Weir|page=122|passage='Wanting the hat,' continues my '''author''', Kirstie, whom I but haltingly follow, for she told this tale like one inspired, 'wanting guns, for there wasna twa grains o' pouder in the house, wi' nae mair weepons than their sticks into their hands, the fower o' them took the road.|translation=[T]here wasn't two grains of powder in the house, with no more weapons than their sticks into their hands, the four of them took the road.}}
# {{senseid|en|cause}} {{lb|en|figurative}} The creator or cause of anything.
#* {{RQ:Burroughs Return of Tarzan|page=132|passage=The other, standing nearly head-on toward the hunters, had not proved so good a mark, and though every spear struck not one entered the great heart. For a moment the huge bull stood trumpeting in rage and pain, casting about with its little eyes for the '''author''' of its hurt.}}

